Subject: [PATCH] changelog + sha256 pins

Start CHANGELOG.md (Keep a Changelog format; v1 / v2 / Unreleased)
and pin the libslang-vk FetchContent by content hash instead of by
release tag.

The fetch is now the tarball of the exact commit the M4.05 milestone
tag points at (fa65b6d5), verified by URL_HASH SHA256 at configure
time. A tag can be re-pointed or its archive regenerated upstream; a
hash cannot drift. Same tested content as before (26/26 ctest,
byte-exact goldens) - a supply-chain hardening change only.

README-VK.md's requirements section now documents the pinning scheme.

Verified: fresh configure + full build from the URL fetch (hash check
enforced by FetchContent); lavapipe smoke on the resulting binary 8/8
(-vkcapture 240 channel regression still passes, -vkbase 2 honored,
-vkdebug zero validation messages).
